          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "The checks have found concrete corrections. The Jensen theorem uses the square of the verified height and does not identify the proposed compatibility margin. Polymath already gives a heat-dependent zero-count estimate, which Claude’s proposed formula omits. The attraction calculation also appears to count individual zeros as conjugate pairs. These change the proposed priorities, although the warning about losing cancellation remains useful.\n"
            ]
